<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχετ-ηγός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>conducting</i> or <i>drawing off water by a
			ditch</i> or <i>conduit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δ᾽ ὅτ᾽ ἀνὴρ ὀ. ἀπὸ κρήνης
					μελανύδρου ἂμ φυτὰ καὶ κήπους ὕδατι ῥόον
					ἡγεμονεύῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.257
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα ὀ.</span>, of the
			flute, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.505.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑῶν ὀ. ἐρώτων</span>, of the
			Alpheus, ib.<i><span class="en">
				362.5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.284
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρως ὀ. ἀνίης</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				228
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
